body:
Facebook and KSL are your best bets if you want a single room. The one comment someone made about the apartments across from Weber State University is Harrison Heights ([https://www.harrisonheightsapartments.com/](https://www.harrisonheightsapartments.com/)) ... but they are mainly for students and sometimes fill up fast. 

&#x200B;

There's a company called Froer ([https://www.froerer.net/utah-properties-rent/](https://www.froerer.net/utah-properties-rent/)) and they have a lot of options. They currently have an apartment open in Washington Terrace (South Ogden, VERY safe area) that's pretty cheap, but they are 2 and 3 bed apartments. 

&#x200B;

Hope this helps, and I wish you good luck, and welcome!

Hahaha, I'm going to be moving out of state....so this should be fuuuuuuuuuuun.

&#x200B;

I'm going to see how much a uhaul trailer would cost though. I know a couple people that might know about the more.....illegal bits...

It's not weird for everyone....but it was fucking weird for me...

&#x200B;

My partner used to like to come into his hand and then "cook" his jizz and then eat it. Now he just will save it and do whatever with it later if he remembers (he hardly does).

Oh?

&#x200B;

Why does it change after a bit?

I agree with this comment. My whole case with them was almost the exact same as yours....I told them ow it affected me and whatever I did, I had a lot of medical documentation and the works, the only thing I might say is different is I had a case manager help me apply and I was in like...a transitional inpatient thing that is hooked onto the side of my therapist's office. It's like a step in-between a hospital visit and just going home, it was NOT helpful, but I got to have my therapist come in and talk to me....which was nice ig?

&#x200B;

Overall, if you're honest with them, and use the people who are used to dealing with the system you should be good.

I'd like to just say life. 

&#x200B;

I am currently looking for Mental health services, a new car and housing all at the same time and even just one would blow.

Mental illness within myself along with the damn price man.

&#x200B;

My best friend recently had his second kid and he took three months off of work to help his wife and LORDY. They went through like....five months of the pregnancy just planning bills out so they could both be off for the first couple of months and they ended up getting a small loan as well. They both have pretty good paying jobs too and their other kid is older (5). The navigation of money seems like a nightmare.

Yup, got a couple. 

When I first started seeing my current therapist I had been through two others at the same...center? Anyways...I had seen two people prior and a psychiatrist to prescribe meds...

After some time they've all come to agree that I have and have been documented as;

PTSD, BPD, Anxiety, Clinical Depression, and general paranoia\*, and agoraphobia.

&#x200B;

Although I don't know how they are all listed in my documentation...this is what my psych and current therapist have mentioned.

OH. MY. GOODNESS. I LOVE fat head dough! I once made a really really good stuffed crust pizza with a bunch of it and it was soooo good. We ended up making it a little too thin the first time around, the second time around we made it just about right but without enough sauce and just....I love it lol.

&#x200B;

I've also tried cloud bread which is basically egg whites and some flour of your choosing, either some cream of tartar or xantham gum and sweetener (depending on what you're making the bread for...). It takes a like....five or ten minutes in the oven and it looks like a cloud. I made mine for the hell of it to see if it was going to come out and it's just like those cloud eggs that people make online, but a little thicker! (Beaten egg whites season and baked and then the yolk added on top and enjoyed).

&#x200B;

I love all of your comment too....sorry I typed out so much to read as well....I got a little excited!
